From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Evan Maddock <maddock.evan@vivaldi.net>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:40:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] backport: Bump webpki-roots and rustls-webpki

This removes the compromised emSign ECC Root CA.

The impact is limited:

* The app uses TLS pinning for non-obfuscated API traffic, so it is
  unaffected.
* Downloading installers for updates could be affected by this, but the
  loader and app reject invalid sha256 checksums, so modifying
  installers is not possible.
* Encrypted DNS proxy relies on webpki. A MITM can observe or proxy
  encrypted TLS traffic, equivalent to observing non-obfuscated API
  packets.

Backported from ba88e0570ff01e6ebba6562d0d1617f2207d677e

Signed-off-by: Evan Maddock <maddock.evan@vivaldi.net>
---
